A first 3.4.1 ascension after taking some time off to deal more fully 
with real life and some time taken to look at writing a Rog-O-Matic for 
nethack. Finally decided I needed to do an ascension to stay current so 
I would be ready for the DevNull tournament. The following was the 
record I made while doing the ascension. A few notes in [] are some 
comments made in retrospect after I finished.
   --Mark
-------------------

YAAP maniac-Wiz-Gno-Mal-Neu

After eight YASD's with monks, I started in a pretty annoyed state. I
can get a monk easily through the Mines and Sokoban, but die preparing
for the Castle. Decided to try a wizard again to play an "easy"
game. In retrospect, it was pretty easy though I never found a BoH nor
magic lamp, and with 24 spells - didn't get identify, fireball, nor
zone of cold.

DL 1 is uneventful. DL 2 has the mine entrance (lit), large general
store and vault. The store has a lot of loot, but nothing really
special except for +3 speed boots. Hmm. Vladamir is now a cat, perhaps
I should go get a pick. Got a pick pretty quickly, but Vlad somehow
found a trap door. Went down a level to find it and back to DL 2.

Have about 700 Zm on DL 2, DL 4 has a potion shop and vault as well.
Left with over 2500 Zm.  Made to Mine Town safely. The temple is cross
aligned. After talking to the priest, AC now -5. A couple armor items
from a dwarf and watchman drop that to AC:-9. A nymph showed up and I
was stupid by zapping it (and broke the mirror).

Went on down to Mine End. Got rid of a second nymph, but it had no
looking glass (sigh). Mine End was the wine cellar. Found a touchstone
as well as the luckstone. (hoping my bad luck is already gone...).
Smoky turns out to be booze. Going up burdened. Back to Mine Town
safely. Read a couple low level spell books. Started up to bring the
loot to the main dungeon (two trips).

Back in the main dungeon and going down. DL 6 is the oracle. Into
Sokoban. Went pretty smoothly - got the amulet of reflection and put
it on. Named my other amulet as "life saving". Burdened again w/
loot and still no bag. Continuing down.

DL 8 has another liquor store. DL 9 has another general store. Still
on the border with burdening, keeping several stashes to stay
speedy. Another general store and a cross aligned altar on DL 10; need
a monster to convert it.  Now have a sack. Also have a vault, let's
look for it - found quickly, now have 2900 Zm (plus stashes). DL 12
has a vault and a huge leprechaun hall (over 13k Zm). DL 13
has the portal. DL 14 and 15 are uneventful.

DL 16 has a nurse though I had to keep it away from my pets.... DL 16
also has a throne room. DL 17 is a rogue level. Lost two pets on these
two levels. DL 18 has a vault, but no portal to Ludios. A can of
grease used to protect several items. Lost my last pet to an invisible
Xorn. DL 19 has a zoo including a gray and blue dragon. The blue
dragon provided scales and electricity resistance (and satiated). A
little excitement from an Olog Hai, had to leave the area twice. The
gray dragon shot itself several times and finally left scales.

DL 20 finally has another temple, but cross aligned again. DL 21 has a
vault. DL 22 has a graveyard and a vault. DL 23 has Medusa but no
titan. I visited the graveyard and lured a few wraiths to DL
21. Welcome to XL:13. Unfortunately, a bone devil read a cursed create
monster & filled the area (including an Elven king). I made it out,
but it is certainly not very safe right now. I have plenty of power
but not very powerful spells. Let's go up and improve my stuff and see
if I have a good spell to use. Still need to find a unicorn. Still
need to convert an altar.

Hmm. Find a c on DL 20. Let's see what I can do first & then try to
bring it quickly to DL 22 to clean up. Made it back to DL
10. Converted the altar after three uses of the bag of tricks (zombie,
lawful unicorn [its a lawful altar], and lynx). Did the conversion w/
lynx, prayed, then sacrificed the unicorn. The zombie stayed where it
died. While BUC testing, the cockatrice figurine is blessed! [but I
never used it...]

Made it back to DL 2 w/ my first cache but with just a sack, are
stressed or worse. Taking three burdened trips to consolidate on DL
10. Sacrificed an Elf Lord and received Magicbane. Finally got my
stuff down and Id'd. Made a big pile of holy water and blessed the key
items. Made some full healing to boost my HP to 142. Magicbane is now
+3. Only one enchant armor so far. Need to search more / get a magic
marker.

Decided to go down and make sure I didn't miss anything / check out
the first level of the quest. With Magicbane, the first level was a
piece of cake. Still need to get to XL 14. Save the game and think
about this tomorrow.

Much better. Went down and took on the horde on DL 22 with a c
corpse. Five swings, four monsters down; one surprised me by using a
lizard to become more limber. The rest of the monsters went down
pretty easily. Brought a few more wraiths to DL 21 and finally welcome
to XL:14 and XL:15 (you feel sensitive). Cleaned the rest of the level
and went back to the quest. A succubus on the way up brought XL:16.

The quest is pretty uneventful. Picked up a couple new spell books on
the way through. The Dark One was actually pretty fun for a little
while. Summoned a black dragon & cockatrice after I walked back to the
up stairs. The worst was a master mind flayer though - needless to say
I'm glad I greased my helmet. The c corpse took care of the random
monsters summoned. The black dragon took care of the rest (I had
reflection...). The Dark One went down to four hits with Magicbane (as
well as catching curses). Only one Id'd item cursed, and a couple
others from blessed to uncursed (easy to fix). The black dragon corpse
made me firm.

On the way back down towards medusa, I found a nurse to boost HP
another 10 or so. Hmm. No levitation, water walking, nor wand of
cold. Let's teleport back to Sokoban / walk back to the cache and see
what I have to use.... Found I have a levitation potion, a wand of
cold (0:7), and a bunch of other loot. A few sacrifices brought a few
more clovers.

Back to the Medusa level. Six zaps with a cold wand spanned the
gap. The RNG is toying with me - Perseus had a sack with a levitation
spell book. Going down, I need better armor. I did a Minotaur test &
dropped 60 HP before it died. DL 25 has rooms w/ a temple, cross
aligned. DL 26 has the castle, a quick check shows a golden naga, and
the usual group of monsters. No high liches nor titans. Make a careful
path to the center, killing an invisible hill giant w/ a tin wand and
now I'm invisible too.

I took a boulder and filled the gap / blasted the drawbridge to avoid
an instant kill. I used a series of spells / retreat / recover to
clean out the main room without any serious damage (and no curses). I
will have a lot of loot to check through / carry to the DL 25
temple. The silver dragon on the back hall left scales - will swap
"real soon now". A red dragon gave me a chill (thought I had that
already, but ate it to be sure).

Wishes - 2 blessed charging scrolls, +3 blessed fixed gauntlets of
dexterity (got +0), +3 blessed fixed helm of brilliance (got +3) and
two magic markers. Will save the last two (1 fast, 1 slow) wishes for
later. [never used...]

Hmm. The back room had a +1 blessed robe. Maybe I'll stick with GDSM &
"oR plus the robe to improve my spell casting rates. Grr. A mmf showed
up on DL 25, need to get rid of it (done). A few other monsters showed
up, let's clean up before going briefly into the VotD so I can
teleport to Sokoban & back again. Fixed up the armor to AC:-31. Still
can recharge both magic markers.

Cleaned out the VotD and started down each level. Juiblex was on DL 31
and went down without hitting me (nor swallowing). Really annoying w/o
reliable water walking / levitation. I had to use a spell to make it
across the last segment and wait for it to time out. Asmodeus is on DL
33. Baalzebub on DL 34. Grr. A doppleganger showed up while I was
trying to visit a nurse. Risky I know, I decided to pass on the
nurse. Orcus is on DL 38, one of the stores had a bag - need to id
it. Grr. An arch lich summoned fled up about four levels, have to get
later.

Rodney is on DL 39. Grr. Even with magic mapping, I somehow missed the
entrance to Vlad's. DL 45 is the end of Gehennom. Found the VS on the
other side, marked it with fire & boulder and started up to look for
Vlad's. On DL 38 (Orcus Town), a master lich showed up and summoned
some pets. They went down quickly, I had to make it to the up stairs
before I could finally kill the ML. Found Vlad's entrance on DL
35. Vlad went down pretty quickly and his chest had another "oR. Back
to Orcus Town to collect some stuff, then back to my cache to do some
more identifying, clean up, sacrificing. A create monster spellbook,
detect treasure, detect unseen, sleep, knock, teleport, a few
others....

Went back to the VS and dropped the bell and candelabra (with
candles). Went to Rodney's tower and it took forever to clean out the
zoo (summoned monsters) though a couple black dragons took out the
L's. A mmf got through when I wasn't looking, took some level info but
no important spells. Had to go back to the stash since I forgot light,
force bolt, and extra heal (over 40k turns). Tried to sac for more
stuff and got a clover & telepathy [sigh].

Back to Rodney's tower. He went down to the FoD after teleporting
next to me over land. Down with the book. Did the invocation. Made it
through the graveyard without waking anyone and locked the door
behind. That didn't help much - the priests and a nalfenshee woke
everybody up and some monster broke the door anyway. Took another long
period to get to the temple. The priest went down to the FoD, an arch
lich lasted a little longer until it summoned a c; turned that into a
corpse and was able to rest a while.

Alternated with magicbane, and the c corpse to leave the lowest level
without any problem. I also gained XL 17 on the way back out. I
refreshed the c corpse about 4 times before leaving Gehennom. The
mysterious force was not too bad - kicked in on 41->42, 39->39, 34->33,
31->31, and that was it. Rodney sent in monsters on DL 33 (refreshed
by c corpse), 31 (another stupid mmf, more mind loss), and came
himself twice. Almost starved on the level above the castle - was weak
before I reached the ground because a levitation spell (to bypass the
trap doors) took too long to wear off.

Made it safely back to the cache to pick up some confusion potions,
gold detect, and refresh a spell. Back up pretty much without
problem and left the main dungeon.

Earth was as simple as usual. Air was a pain - I thought that a slow
monster spell would expel you from an air elemental; that didn't
work.... I used one full heal after the 200+ HP air elemental dropped
me down to about 120. Water was boring and I started to forget detect
monster as I was crossing it. After three K rations, finally made it
to Astral.

Death to right, Pestilence in the middle, and Famine to the left. A
master lich came to meet me and brought some pets to play with. Went
through the horde to the middle altar (lawful). Fought my way back and
went left - altar to Thoth (neutral). Offered the amulet to get...

